    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "**Question:** What is polymorphism?"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Short Answer"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Polymorphism allows objects of different types to be treated through the same interface. Enables writing generic code that works with derived types."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Detailed Explanation"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Polymorphism means 'many forms'. Achieved through method overriding (runtime) and method overloading (compile-time). Enables extensible, maintainable code."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Example"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "data": {
        "title": "Polymorphism Example",
        "language": "csharp",
        "code": "public class Shape {\n    public virtual void Draw() => Console.WriteLine(\"Drawing shape\");\n}\npublic class Circle : Shape {\n    public override void Draw() => Console.WriteLine(\"Drawing circle\");\n}\nShape s = new Circle();\ns.Draw(); // Calls Circle.Draw()"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
